From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Harry Turton <harrisonturton@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 19:18:06 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Add parse_all_errors, going on past syntax and lexer errors

The parser stopped at the first syntax error, and a lexer error ended the
file. After a syntax error, parsing now goes on from the next statement
at the file's top level, and lexing goes on past a lexer error.
parse_all_errors fails with every error found, in the order they appear;
parse still fails with the first.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01H2KN4B9EK4GzM2uqpms4ft
